 "circuits": [
  {
   "id": "typical",
   "title": "Typical application, stereo with microcontroller mute and standby",
   "page": 1,
   "description": "Two non-inverting channels on ±VS, each with 18 kΩ feedback over 560 Ω to ground and an AC-coupled input. Pin 5 sits at the collector of an NPN transistor whose collector load is 15 kΩ to +VS, filtered by 1 µF to +VS. A 5 V microcontroller drives the transistor base and the bottom of a 15 kΩ emitter resistor; an 18 kΩ emitter resistor goes to ground. With the base low the collector current stops and pin 5 rises to +VS (standby); the emitter current sets how far pin 5 drops below +VS, choosing mute or play. Each output has 4.7 Ω in series with 100 nF to ground; each supply rail has 1000 µF to ground.",
   "parts": [
